The destroy armour spell used by Sporkhack's wizardly spellcasters
removes any fooproofing from the affected piece of armour, then applies
a number of damage levels to it.  If you have MR, the number of damage
levels applied is always exactly one; otherwise it may be as many as
three.  If the armour is already thoroughly damaged, it is instead
destroyed.

>"Gee, you've GOT the intrinsics that let your PC
>walk over monsters that used to kill your PC, guess
>we'd better change the game to cripple those
>intrinsics so all kinds of monsters are always
>dangerous."

In Sporkhack, many kinds of monsters cease to be dangerous to high-level
characters. A level 10 sporkhack character with PR (or MC 3) and AC -5
still regards most of the denizens of the mines as either armoured
feather dusters or glass cannons, just as a level 10 Nethack character
similarly equipped does.

However, the game has been adjusted so that certain monsters (such as
dragons) which it is felt ought to be at least moderately threatening to
everyone actually *are* at least moderately threatening to everyone. In
vanilla, a dragon is a greasy smear on the windscreen if you have
reflection; in spork, a dragon at range will act as a slow drain on your
HP unless you also have the resistance.
